"{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.33767/osf.io/dz3tn_v1\",\n  \"title\": \"A Structural-Semiotic Analysis of the Comb Sign M176 in the Indus Script as a Referent Category Classifier - A Hypothesis\",\n  \"authors\": \"Inderjeet Singh\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<p>This article gives a structural-semiotic analysis of the comb sign (Sign 176 in Mahadevan's 1977 concordance) in the Indus script, and advances the methodological argument that semiotics constitutes a necessary complement to epigraphy in the study of undeciphered scripts. Epigraphy asks what a sign says in the language it encodes, on the other hand Semiotics asks what a sign does in the sign system, a question that can be answered without phonological decipherment. Drawing on Sampson (1985), Harris (1986, 2000), and Coulmas (1989), the article grounds this distinction theoretically and demonstrates it through three semiotic frameworks applied to the comb sign: Peirce’s triadic model of icon, index, and symbol; Saussure’s syntagmatic and paradigmatic analysis; and Barthes’ denotation, connotation, and myth. These frameworks support the hypothesis, first advanced by Mahadevan (1982, 2006, 2012), that Sign 176 probably functions as a referent category classifier, though the category it encodes could not be determined without decipherment.The contributions of this article are of theoretical and methodological nature. It is perhaps the first simultaneous application of all three classical semiotic frameworks to a single Indus sign. Secondly, only a few previous studies appear to have formulated explicitly the methodological complementarity of semiotics and epigraphy in Indus script research, this article advances that thesis in grounded form. It also tries to offer what appears to be probably the first structured cross-cultural comparative analysis of classifier sign function across the Egyptian, Mesopotamian, and Indus traditions on the basis of existing literature. Fourthly, it advances a new cross-linguistic cognitive motivation argument for the referent category classifier hypothesis. The article additionally suggests that the Indus sign system may have functioned as a professionally restricted administrative notation. No decipherment claims are advanced.</p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.33767/osf.io/dz3tn_v1\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2026-05-23T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.33767/osf.io/dz3tn_v1\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"posted-content\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Center for Open Science', 'container_title': '', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'posted-content', 'member': '15934', 'prefix': '10.33767'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctvzgb7m5.8\",\n  \"title\": \"The Buddhist Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctvzgb7m5.8\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2020-03-26T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvzgb7m5.8\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Harrassowitz Verlag', 'container_title': 'The Buddhist Indus Script and Scriptures', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '9-64', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"title\": \"The Indus Valley Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2015-02-06T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.9\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'The Archaeology and Epigraphy of Indus Writing', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '4-12', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix': '10.2307'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2139/ssrn.4900721\",\n  \"title\": \"Deciphering Indus script and Pashupati Seal of Indus Valley Civilization\",\n  \"authors\": \"Shahbaig Kahoor Khan\",\n  \"abstract\": \"<jats:p>Indus Valley Civilization is one of the left out archaeological treasures, that is being ignored in the recent times. This paper is a guide to the scholars and the archaeologist, which will help them to solve the mysteries of the ancient Indus Civilization and its Script. The paper includes thorough research observations on the interpretation of the scripts. Among the script and the famous Pashupati seal has also been thoroughly interpreted and explained. This could be a guide to interpret Indus customs and culture more nearer to the truth of past. The political controversies altering the history of Indus can cause a tremendous if not correctly study.</jats:p>\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2139/ssrn.4900721\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2024-01-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4900721\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"posted-content\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 1,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Elsevier BV', 'container_title': '', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'posted-content', 'member': '78', 'prefix': '10.2139'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.1080/0161-118891862873\",\n  \"title\": \"A FREQUENCY ANALYSIS OF THE INDUS SCRIPT\",\n  \"authors\": \"Subhash C. Kak\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.1080/0161-118891862873\",\n  \"published_date\": \"1988-07-01T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.1080/0161-118891862873\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 6,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Informa UK Limited', 'container_title': 'Cryptologia', 'volume': '12', 'issue': '3', 'page': '129-143', 'issn': ['0161-1194', '1558-1586'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '301', 'prefix': '10.1080'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"title\": \"Sanskrit Influence on the Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"Jeyakumar Ramasami\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2025-12-20T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.21275/sr251216111751\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"journal-article\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'International Journal of Science and Research', 'container_title': 'International Journal of Science and Research (IJSR)', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '1329-1334', 'issn': ['2319-7064'], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'journal-article', 'member': '8810', 'prefix': '10.21275'}\"\n}\n{\n  \"paper_id\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.14\",\n  \"title\": \"Proto-Dravidian and the Indus Script\",\n  \"authors\": \"\",\n  \"abstract\": \"\",\n  \"doi\": \"10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.14\",\n  \"published_date\": \"2015-02-06T00:00:00\",\n  \"pdf_url\": \"\",\n  \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.2307/j.ctvr43jmf.14\",\n  \"source\": \"crossref\",\n  \"updated_date\": \"\",\n  \"categories\": \"book-chapter\",\n  \"keywords\": \"\",\n  \"citations\": 0,\n  \"references\": \"\",\n  \"extra\": \"{'publisher': 'Archaeopress Publishing Ltd', 'container_title': 'The Archaeology and Epigraphy of Indus Writing', 'volume': '', 'issue': '', 'page': '77-99', 'issn': [], 'isbn': [], 'crossref_type': 'book-chapter', 'member': '1121', 'prefix':